# Build context excludes for deploy/web/Dockerfile.web (context: repo root).
#
# Without this file, `COPY . .` copies whatever happens to be sitting in the
# working tree -- including node_modules, which is never wanted here: the
# build stage does its own `pnpm install` fresh inside the container, and
# copying a host-installed node_modules on top would be both very slow
# (potentially minutes, especially over a slow bind-mounted filesystem, e.g.
# a WSL2 /mnt/c/ path) and could clobber the container's own install with
# host-specific artifacts. Keep this in sync with the spirit of .gitignore,
# though the two files serve different purposes and don't need to match
# exactly.
#
# .pnpm-store is the same story but easy to miss: running `pnpm install`
# against this repo from inside a container (e.g. to test/build on a host
# with no Node/pnpm) can leave a *local* content-addressable store behind
# at the repo root instead of using pnpm's usual global one, tens of
# thousands of tiny files -- exactly the worst case for slow bind-mount I/O,
# and it silently defeats the node_modules exclusion above by re-copying an
# equivalent amount of data under a different name.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.git

# Build outputs -- rebuilt inside the container, never wanted from the host
dist
**/dist
build
out
release
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test artifacts
coverage
test-results
playwright-report

# Local/editor state
.DS_Store
*.local
.env
.env.*
.claude
.agents
.vitepress
